# Homework 2 holes: empty the tracing recorders and the two endpoints.
#
# Apply from the repository root:
#
#     git apply homework/module-1/hw2-holes.patch
#
# This removes the body of five functions and leaves every signature and
# docstring in place:
#
#   observability/instrument.py  record_tool_result
#                                _set_permission_denied_attributes
#                                record_activity
#   server/app.py                create_session
#                                post_message
#
# Unlike the Homework 1 holes, these stop the agent running until you fill
# them, and that is deliberate. agent/agent.py's _call seam absorbs a
# NotImplementedError from a *tool*, because a half-built agent that still
# holds a conversation is useful. It does not absorb one from a *recorder*: an
# instrumentation layer that failed quietly would leave a partially recorded
# event log, and a log that is wrong is worse than a log that is missing.
#
# Expect tests/test_observability.py to go red. Run the hole tests with
# --runxfail to see each contract on its own:
#
#     uv run pytest --runxfail tests/test_hw_holes.py -k hw2
#     uv run pytest --runxfail -vv tests/test_hw_holes.py -k create_session_binds
#
# Needs the agent extra: uv sync --extra agent
#
# To undo, whatever state your copy is in:
#
#     git checkout -- observability/instrument.py server/app.py
#
# Generated from 5d6eddf. If either file changes, regenerate rather than
# hand-editing.
